01:01:20.785 --> 01:01:22.530
'Cause obviously, you get sad,

01:01:22.530 --> 01:01:24.958
you get those days where
you don't wanna do anything

01:01:24.958 --> 01:01:26.430
and you're a little not fun-
- You sure you're here?

01:01:26.430 --> 01:01:28.090
- Kinda not fun to be around,

01:01:28.090 --> 01:01:29.140
obviously, I'm not going to show that.

01:01:29.140 --> 01:01:31.430
But then it's like, am I
lying by not showing that?

01:01:31.430 --> 01:01:32.600
Like, I don't know, I hate this.

01:01:32.600 --> 01:01:33.967
- Exactly.
- So uncomfortable.

01:01:33.967 --> 01:01:36.270
- 'Cause I feel like that
when there's a camera,

01:01:36.270 --> 01:01:38.150
I feel like I have to be
in like the good mode,

01:01:38.150 --> 01:01:40.300
the entertaining mode where sometimes,

01:01:40.300 --> 01:01:43.950
you just don't feel like
being entertaining or talking.

01:01:43.950 --> 01:01:45.760
- I just got to like take
the smile pill, right?

01:01:45.760 --> 01:01:49.150
And like, I'm on camera now, hey!

01:01:49.150 --> 01:01:51.190
Yeah, it's tough.

01:01:51.190 --> 01:01:54.790
And I feel like I can completely see why,

01:01:54.790 --> 01:01:56.550
especially on the YouTubers, right?

01:01:56.550 --> 01:01:58.640
Why there is kind of
been this like kind of,

01:01:58.640 --> 01:02:01.000
I've almost seen as like a growing thing

01:02:01.000 --> 01:02:03.610
of faceless YouTubers,
just because I think

01:02:03.610 --> 01:02:07.550
people are starting to realize
the kind of, not risk per se,

01:02:07.550 --> 01:02:10.620
but the demerits to like showing your face

01:02:10.620 --> 01:02:13.120
and showing your self on camera.

01:02:13.120 --> 01:02:14.070
- It's way more pressure.

01:02:14.070 --> 01:02:15.089
And I've noticed that since,

01:02:15.089 --> 01:02:18.020
because I started off with most people

01:02:18.020 --> 01:02:21.210
not knowing much about me,
and then Trash Taste started,

01:02:21.210 --> 01:02:23.210
and now I'm on camera every week.

01:02:23.210 --> 01:02:25.067
And it's something that I
just haven't been used to.

01:02:25.067 --> 01:02:26.120
- I'm so lazy.

01:02:26.120 --> 01:02:27.190
I just can't be bothered

01:02:27.190 --> 01:02:29.460
going through all the effort
of like hiding my identity.

01:02:29.460 --> 01:02:31.620
- But yeah, like I said earlier, though,

01:02:31.620 --> 01:02:33.530
I think the Japanese industry-
- They like that?

01:02:33.530 --> 01:02:34.530
- The entertainment industry

01:02:34.530 --> 01:02:36.750
used to be very sort of strict,

01:02:36.750 --> 01:02:40.708
and they expected you to sort
of portray an artist's image,

01:02:40.708 --> 01:02:42.570
like idols and-
_ Like it was a,

01:02:42.570 --> 01:02:44.000
it would be a bit huge scandal, right,

01:02:44.000 --> 01:02:45.586
if they were dating someone.
- Exactly.

01:02:45.586 --> 01:02:47.710
But thanks to YouTube and like,

01:02:47.710 --> 01:02:50.650
this recent sort of generation,

01:02:50.650 --> 01:02:53.560
a lot of musicians and entertainers

01:02:53.560 --> 01:02:55.276
are starting to become YouTubers.

01:02:55.276 --> 01:02:58.730
And I think that's a huge
plus because they're realizing

01:02:58.730 --> 01:03:01.400
that they can be themselves
more and still work.

01:03:01.400 --> 01:03:03.070
- And be human, right?
- Yeah, and be human.

01:03:03.070 --> 01:03:06.030
And people are actually
looking for that now.

01:03:06.030 --> 01:03:10.890
And so this is a huge, a big sort of plus

01:03:10.890 --> 01:03:12.290
for the entertainment industry,

01:03:12.290 --> 01:03:14.230
and I think it's a good change for us.

01:03:14.230 --> 01:03:17.640
And I feel it's a chance for
us to be more of ourselves

01:03:17.640 --> 01:03:22.640
and to really put out our
own messages into our work.

01:03:22.900 --> 01:03:24.100
- Did you have any control

01:03:24.100 --> 01:03:26.270
over your own like artist's image,

01:03:26.270 --> 01:03:28.308
or was that all-
- Not at the beginning.

01:03:28.308 --> 01:03:29.968
This is my first time
actually talking about this,

01:03:29.968 --> 01:03:31.048
and I would love to talk about it.

01:03:31.048 --> 01:03:32.935
- A Trash Taste exclusive!
- Let's go,

01:03:32.935 --> 01:03:34.368
let's go.
- Exclusive.

01:03:34.368 --> 01:03:37.330
No, but everything in the
beginning of my career,

01:03:37.330 --> 01:03:39.570
because I was completely an amateur.

01:03:39.570 --> 01:03:41.930
I wasn't, like usually rock artists

01:03:41.930 --> 01:03:44.940
start doing their stuff
before their debut.

01:03:44.940 --> 01:03:46.290
Like they do small lives venues,

01:03:46.290 --> 01:03:48.880
they do tours, they have a fan base.

01:03:48.880 --> 01:03:52.210
But for me, like day one that my fans

01:03:53.860 --> 01:03:56.550
made a debut with me
was my day one as well.

01:03:56.550 --> 01:03:58.240
And I didn't do lives before that.

01:03:58.240 --> 01:04:00.420
I didn't have media coverage
or anything out there.

01:04:00.420 --> 01:04:02.200
So it was just Niconico.

01:04:02.200 --> 01:04:07.200
And so I needed aid, I needed direction.

01:04:07.490 --> 01:04:12.490
And so my director made
sort of this image of who,

01:04:13.080 --> 01:04:14.670
what kind of artist I should be.

01:04:14.670 --> 01:04:19.630
And I tried to sort of be
that, I said that I could.

01:04:19.630 --> 01:04:21.233
So in the beginning though,

01:04:22.200 --> 01:04:25.480
everything was completely like, you know-

01:04:25.480 --> 01:04:27.670
- Decided for you?
- Yes, decided for me.

01:04:27.670 --> 01:04:30.420
And I didn't even know what
I wanted yet as a musician.

01:04:30.420 --> 01:04:33.530
So I couldn't say, hey,
I wanna do this, I wanna,

01:04:33.530 --> 01:04:36.160
I just wanted to sing, that's
all that I wanted to do.

01:04:36.160 --> 01:04:38.480
- And that's how it normally
is. Artists just kind of,

01:04:38.480 --> 01:04:39.890
a lot of thing I noticed about artists

01:04:39.890 --> 01:04:41.460
is that they just wanna focus on the art,

01:04:41.460 --> 01:04:44.350
and they have no idea about
how to market themselves

01:04:44.350 --> 01:04:45.633
or branding.
- So it really helped me

01:04:45.633 --> 01:04:49.681
to have the direction and
to be told, like, you know,

01:04:49.681 --> 01:04:52.390
everything other than
the singing part to do,

01:04:52.390 --> 01:04:53.580
how to do this, how to do that.

01:04:53.580 --> 01:04:55.960
They taught me about the
entertainment industry,

01:04:55.960 --> 01:04:57.220
they taught me how to do lives,

01:04:57.220 --> 01:05:00.085
they taught me how to
take artist's photographs.

01:05:00.085 --> 01:05:01.150
They taught me everything.

01:05:01.150 --> 01:05:02.366
- God, I wish I knew that.

01:05:02.366 --> 01:05:05.020
- Yeah, we just kind of
had to learn on the job

01:05:05.020 --> 01:05:08.240
and take an array of
the most awkward photos

01:05:08.240 --> 01:05:09.320
that have ever been taken.
- But in the beginning,

01:05:09.320 --> 01:05:11.430
it was so sad because
I didn't show my face,

01:05:11.430 --> 01:05:12.900
but I had to take artist's photographs.

01:05:12.900 --> 01:05:14.872
So I was always wearing a hood.

01:05:14.872 --> 01:05:17.650
And so I was like standing
in front of the camera

01:05:17.650 --> 01:05:19.690
wearing a hood and not showing my face.

01:05:19.690 --> 01:05:21.591
And I was like, you know, this could be-

01:05:21.591 --> 01:05:22.424
- Anyone else could do it.
- Anyone else.

01:05:22.424 --> 01:05:25.453
It could be a mannequin
and no one would notice.

01:05:25.453 --> 01:05:27.770
Does it have to be me?

01:05:27.770 --> 01:05:28.603
That kind of thing.

01:05:28.603 --> 01:05:30.700
Even in my promotion videos,
I didn't show my face,

01:05:30.700 --> 01:05:32.150
and so my neck was always like this,

01:05:32.150 --> 01:05:33.340
and by the end of the video,

01:05:33.340 --> 01:05:34.990
I'd be like, oh my neck, my neck.

01:05:37.430 --> 01:05:39.530
So that happened behind the cameras.

01:05:39.530 --> 01:05:40.760
And there were a lot of things

01:05:40.760 --> 01:05:42.470
that were difficult in the beginning.

01:05:42.470 --> 01:05:45.650
But now that I think about
it, it was really funny.

01:05:45.650 --> 01:05:47.620
It was really funny and fun.

01:05:47.620 --> 01:05:50.730
And it helped me learn
about a lot of things.

01:05:50.730 --> 01:05:52.454
- Did you have, did you
ever have that point

01:05:52.454 --> 01:05:54.340
where you had to like
work on your signature,

01:05:54.340 --> 01:05:56.170
or did you have a good looking signature

01:05:56.170 --> 01:05:57.620
to begin with when you sign things?

01:05:57.620 --> 01:06:00.730
- I just use, I still use to this day,

01:06:00.730 --> 01:06:03.160
just a regular, like cursive signature.

01:06:03.160 --> 01:06:04.230
- I'm so jealous.

01:06:04.230 --> 01:06:06.140
- I literally just do like four circles,

01:06:06.140 --> 01:06:07.710
and I'm like, bam, bon appetit.

01:06:07.710 --> 01:06:10.390
- I would love to have a
cool looking signature,

01:06:10.390 --> 01:06:12.182
but I don't know how to
do it because I never-

01:06:12.182 --> 01:06:13.420
- I think Joey out of all of us

01:06:13.420 --> 01:06:15.340
has the coolest looking signature.

01:06:15.340 --> 01:06:17.490
- Which is hilarious, because I came off,

01:06:17.490 --> 01:06:18.323
that signature-
- Really, show me

01:06:18.323 --> 01:06:20.500
your signature.
- My signature?

01:06:20.500 --> 01:06:21.550
Do we have like a thing?

01:06:21.550 --> 01:06:23.380
'Cause like I came up with my signature,

01:06:23.380 --> 01:06:25.794
I think, in like, it was the
first con I ever went to.

01:06:25.794 --> 01:06:26.990
It was basically the first time

01:06:26.990 --> 01:06:28.290
I ever had to sign something.

01:06:28.290 --> 01:06:29.900
Like someone came up to me and was like-

01:06:29.900 --> 01:06:31.890
- And you made up-
- Hey, man, I love your work.

01:06:31.890 --> 01:06:32.860
Can you sign something?

01:06:32.860 --> 01:06:35.720
And I'm like, who the fuck
wants a signature from me?

01:06:35.720 --> 01:06:36.895
- You made that up on the spot?

01:06:36.895 --> 01:06:37.730
- I made that up on the
spot and I was like,

01:06:37.730 --> 01:06:39.770
you know what, good enough.

01:06:39.770 --> 01:06:42.520
This is just gonna be my
signature for the rest of my life.

01:06:42.520 --> 01:06:43.700
- 'Cause while Joey is
doing his signature,

01:06:43.700 --> 01:06:45.750
because I remember the first time

01:06:45.750 --> 01:06:47.480
I got asked to do my signature,

01:06:47.480 --> 01:06:51.060
I looked like a lost deer in headlights.

01:06:51.060 --> 01:06:52.920
Look at that, that's-

01:06:52.920 --> 01:06:55.580
- That's my signature.
- That looks cool.

01:06:55.580 --> 01:06:57.450
That looks like a proper
artist's signature.

01:06:57.450 --> 01:06:59.043
- I could sell that on Yahoo.

01:07:00.700 --> 01:07:02.190
- Yeah, I literally always like, okay,

01:07:02.190 --> 01:07:05.520
what is like a distinct
thing about a signature?

01:07:05.520 --> 01:07:08.080
Lots of like unnecessarily long lines.

01:07:08.080 --> 01:07:08.980
Lots of like overlap,

01:07:08.980 --> 01:07:11.470
to the point where it needs
to be illegible, basically.

01:07:11.470 --> 01:07:13.110
- Let me show you how it's done, Joey.

01:07:13.110 --> 01:07:14.972
- So show me your signature-

01:07:14.972 --> 01:07:17.287
- Mine I think is in between

01:07:17.287 --> 01:07:18.120
a little of both.
- And I was like, okay,

01:07:18.120 --> 01:07:20.067
I can't just like write The Anime Man.

01:07:20.067 --> 01:07:22.400
(all laugh)

01:07:23.338 --> 01:07:25.888
- I can see that you probably
came up with that in-

01:07:26.795 --> 01:07:27.628
- That seems like-

01:07:27.628 --> 01:07:28.640
- That looks like Cdan.

01:07:31.580 --> 01:07:33.630
- Am I looking at Rorschach image here?

01:07:33.630 --> 01:07:35.120
- Listen, you think when
Picasso was in the museum,

01:07:35.120 --> 01:07:35.953
he had to put up with this shit?

01:07:35.953 --> 01:07:36.790
Listen, let me explain, all right?

01:07:36.790 --> 01:07:39.770
You have the C, the D, and
then I just do whatever.

01:07:39.770 --> 01:07:41.951
It's always like I do the
C and D and I give up.

01:07:41.951 --> 01:07:43.710
- This is like, you know-
- And Garnt's signature?

01:07:43.710 --> 01:07:44.560
- Okay, I'll do it.

01:07:44.560 --> 01:07:45.560
This is like when the kid

01:07:45.560 --> 01:07:46.590
brings back a drawing.
- We have to see yours

01:07:46.590 --> 01:07:47.565
as well.
- Yeah,

01:07:47.565 --> 01:07:48.398
this is like when the kid brings

01:07:48.398 --> 01:07:49.680
like a drawing to their parents

01:07:49.680 --> 01:07:50.720
when they're like three or something

01:07:50.720 --> 01:07:52.480
and the parents have to act impressed.

01:07:52.480 --> 01:07:53.530
Like, oh, you did this?

01:07:53.530 --> 01:07:54.610
Oh, it looks so good.

01:07:54.610 --> 01:07:55.443
- It's not even that.

01:07:55.443 --> 01:07:56.430
It's just like, put it on the phone.

01:07:56.430 --> 01:07:58.150
- When I'm signing the packages in Japan,

01:07:58.150 --> 01:07:59.640
they'll be like, oh,
full signature please.

01:07:59.640 --> 01:08:00.473
And I'm like, oh, of course, of course.

01:08:00.473 --> 01:08:01.523
Then I just do that, and they're like,

01:08:01.523 --> 01:08:03.110
they look at me like, what was that?

01:08:03.110 --> 01:08:04.880
That wasn't full signature.

01:08:04.880 --> 01:08:05.713
- That's mine.

01:08:05.713 --> 01:08:07.070
It's not as good as Joey's, but-

01:08:07.070 --> 01:08:08.160
- That's pretty clean.
- That's pretty clean.

01:08:08.160 --> 01:08:09.648
- It's okay.
- Hold it up to the camera.

01:08:09.648 --> 01:08:11.870
- Show that on camera.
- It's okay, it's okay.

01:08:11.870 --> 01:08:12.703
It's not bad.
- Yeah, see, I can read that

01:08:12.703 --> 01:08:14.240
and be like, yeah, that
clearly says Gigguk.

01:08:14.240 --> 01:08:16.070
I look at this and I'm like, who's Dan?

01:08:16.070 --> 01:08:18.287
- Honestly, this is
cleaned up a lot, because-

01:08:18.287 --> 01:08:19.870
- I have a unique one every time.

01:08:19.870 --> 01:08:21.475
This is bullshit.

01:08:21.475 --> 01:08:22.815
Why would I want this?

01:08:22.815 --> 01:08:23.870
- I thought-
- You wanna do yours

01:08:23.870 --> 01:08:24.960
while we're waiting?
- Okay.

01:08:24.960 --> 01:08:26.410
- I thought one thing that differentiates

01:08:26.410 --> 01:08:28.570
between like a regular signature
and an artist's signature

01:08:28.570 --> 01:08:31.110
is like they have some
kind of like thing in it.

01:08:31.110 --> 01:08:32.940
Yeah, see, that's clean.
- That looks good.

01:08:32.940 --> 01:08:34.400
That looks good.

01:08:34.400 --> 01:08:35.233
- But you know,

01:08:35.233 --> 01:08:36.280
I'm actually looking.
- Wait, wait.

01:08:36.280 --> 01:08:37.113
Put it up to the camera.

01:08:37.113 --> 01:08:37.946
- Put it up to the camera.

01:08:37.946 --> 01:08:39.680
- See that's clean.
- No, I'm actually

01:08:39.680 --> 01:08:42.138
looking for a new signature.

01:08:42.138 --> 01:08:44.913
So you guys can think of one for me.

01:08:45.760 --> 01:08:49.140
- I got you, say no more,
I'll make one for you.

01:08:49.140 --> 01:08:51.770
- So like wait, so-
- Which kind of style

01:08:51.770 --> 01:08:52.980
do you like the most?

01:08:52.980 --> 01:08:55.020
- One hint I need is a lot of like-

01:08:55.020 --> 01:08:56.760
- A lot of squiggles,
I like the squiggles.

01:08:56.760 --> 01:08:58.330
- A lot of pointless lines, right?

01:08:58.330 --> 01:08:59.430
- Monocles, higher IQ.

01:09:00.804 --> 01:09:03.304
- But my name is pretty
difficult to do that with.

01:09:05.150 --> 01:09:06.970
- I mean, just go as cursive as you can.

01:09:06.970 --> 01:09:11.900
You're like, this is, put on
the top hat and the monocle.

01:09:11.900 --> 01:09:13.305
- I go for the doctor note-

01:09:13.305 --> 01:09:15.545
- I kinda like this.
- Yeah, right, see?

01:09:15.545 --> 01:09:17.425
See?
- Yeah, I kind of like,

01:09:17.425 --> 01:09:19.092
Cdan-
- It's my Cdan.

01:09:20.053 --> 01:09:21.380
- Pointing at my signature, by the way,

01:09:21.380 --> 01:09:22.577
you can get that on the record.

01:09:22.577 --> 01:09:24.760
- Yeah, I kind of like this one.

01:09:24.760 --> 01:09:27.950
So maybe I'll just like get rid of the O

01:09:27.950 --> 01:09:29.350
and just go Cnan.

01:09:29.350 --> 01:09:30.183
- Yes.

01:09:31.660 --> 01:09:32.810
- It's more C, I think.

01:09:35.700 --> 01:09:37.951
- I like that.
- That's good.

01:09:37.951 --> 01:09:38.784
- That looks like,

01:09:38.784 --> 01:09:41.370
that looks like it says Chon.
- Chen, Chen.

01:09:41.370 --> 01:09:42.203
- Chen.

01:09:43.370 --> 01:09:44.750
Oh yes, my favorite artist, Chen.

01:09:44.750 --> 01:09:46.225
- I'll have to ask my staff, though,

01:09:46.225 --> 01:09:48.290
if this passes for the-

01:09:48.290 --> 01:09:51.490
- Do you have to get your
signature approved by your staff?

01:09:51.490 --> 01:09:54.033
- Not usually, but in this case, probably.

01:09:54.924 --> 01:09:57.314
- When it's this bad, it's like, oh God.

01:09:57.314 --> 01:09:58.147
- I got to ask,

01:09:58.147 --> 01:10:01.870
have you guys ever had a fan
ask you to redo a signature?

01:10:01.870 --> 01:10:02.703
- Oh yeah, I have.

01:10:02.703 --> 01:10:05.540
- 'Cause I've had that before.

01:10:05.540 --> 01:10:06.900
That's why, because my signature

01:10:06.900 --> 01:10:08.470
looks a lot better than it used to,

01:10:08.470 --> 01:10:11.620
because before, it used to
look something like this.

01:10:11.620 --> 01:10:16.620
And I remember, I put this
on like a guy's shirt,

01:10:16.770 --> 01:10:18.090
'cause he wanted me to sign a shirt,

01:10:18.090 --> 01:10:19.680
and he deadass looks at that,

01:10:19.680 --> 01:10:22.600
and he was like, "Can you
do that again, please?

01:10:22.600 --> 01:10:24.230
I can't read that."

01:10:24.230 --> 01:10:25.670
- I got a good one for
you, can I have the pen?

01:10:25.670 --> 01:10:26.890
- All right.
- So I was at a bar

01:10:26.890 --> 01:10:29.160
with a friend in the
middle of nowhere in Japan.

01:10:29.160 --> 01:10:30.610
And for some reason, he
thought it'd be entertaining

01:10:30.610 --> 01:10:32.820
to tell the person at the
bar that I was a YouTuber.

01:10:32.820 --> 01:10:35.590
I really don't wanna do that.
- I hate it when they do.

01:10:35.590 --> 01:10:37.975
- It's just like, you're not
gonna get it if I show you,

01:10:37.975 --> 01:10:39.470
and you're not, you're
only gonna be impressed

01:10:39.470 --> 01:10:40.703
by the numbers and not
wanting to (indistinct).

01:10:40.703 --> 01:10:42.250
So it's like, don't do it.

01:10:42.250 --> 01:10:44.090
So he does it, anyway,
so I'm like quite drunk,

01:10:44.090 --> 01:10:45.350
and they're like, can you please,

01:10:45.350 --> 01:10:48.007
for some reason they brought
out a shikishi, like 2:00 a.m.,

01:10:48.007 --> 01:10:49.780
and I'm already pretty, I'm pretty drunk.

01:10:49.780 --> 01:10:54.780
So they hand it to me and I'm
trying my best to do this.

01:10:55.220 --> 01:10:57.253
So all I do in the end is just this.

01:10:58.910 --> 01:11:00.477
I do this.

01:11:00.477 --> 01:11:01.310
And they were like, "Whoa!"

01:11:01.310 --> 01:11:02.227
And I'm like looking at my friend,

01:11:02.227 --> 01:11:04.560
I'm like, I can't believe
they're taking that.

01:11:04.560 --> 01:11:06.040
And they put, they hung it up on the wall

01:11:06.040 --> 01:11:06.997
in front of me.
- Really?

01:11:06.997 --> 01:11:08.440
- And I doubt it's still there.

01:11:08.440 --> 01:11:09.380
They must've taken that down.

01:11:09.380 --> 01:11:10.930
- Well, it's like the signature

01:11:10.930 --> 01:11:13.933
that we did at AmiAmi, right?

01:11:15.455 --> 01:11:18.860
AmiAmi is like a figurine store,

01:11:18.860 --> 01:11:20.320
in Akihabara, it's like
one of the biggest ones.

01:11:20.320 --> 01:11:22.450
And at one part of their store,

01:11:22.450 --> 01:11:25.000
they have this, just these massive line

01:11:25.000 --> 01:11:27.720
of like maybe like 50
shikishis from like artists

01:11:27.720 --> 01:11:29.873
and like figurine sculptors
and stuff like that.

01:11:29.873 --> 01:11:31.950
- Like proper mangakas.
- Proper mangakas

01:11:31.950 --> 01:11:33.535
and stuff like that.
- Artists who've been there.

01:11:33.535 --> 01:11:34.368
And we did a video then.

01:11:34.368 --> 01:11:35.700
They were like, "Hey,
can you sign a sikishi

01:11:35.700 --> 01:11:37.320
for us 'cause you filmed here."

01:11:37.320 --> 01:11:39.010
And I didn't take into account,

01:11:39.010 --> 01:11:41.830
I didn't actually think
they were gonna hang it up

01:11:41.830 --> 01:11:43.050
next to all these amazing-
- I just think

01:11:43.050 --> 01:11:45.800
my signature's worth nothing.
- Yeah, right.

01:11:45.800 --> 01:11:47.743
So we were just like,
fuck it, let's just do it.

01:11:47.743 --> 01:11:49.560
They're probably just
saying this to be nice,

01:11:49.560 --> 01:11:50.393
let's just do it.

01:11:50.393 --> 01:11:52.120
Turns out, I went back like a week later,

01:11:52.120 --> 01:11:54.150
it's up there on the wall-
- Oh no.

01:11:54.150 --> 01:11:56.497
- Next to these incredible
looking sikishis,

01:11:56.497 --> 01:12:00.031
and it just looks like absolute dogshit.

01:12:00.031 --> 01:12:00.864
And we're like, fuck, we should have-

01:12:00.864 --> 01:12:03.631
- It's a macaroni art next
to like the Banksy one.

01:12:03.631 --> 01:12:04.750
It's pretty appalling.

01:12:04.750 --> 01:12:06.480
- I was like, fuck, it
was the first time ever,

01:12:06.480 --> 01:12:08.750
I was like, fuck, I wish
they'd just take that down.

01:12:08.750 --> 01:12:09.583
I don't want this clout.

01:12:09.583 --> 01:12:11.400
- It's like that horse meme where you have

01:12:11.400 --> 01:12:13.280
like a really professionally drawn horse,

01:12:13.280 --> 01:12:16.690
and then the last third is
just like a kid's drawing.

01:12:16.690 --> 01:12:18.730
that's our drawing in AmiAmi.

01:12:18.730 --> 01:12:20.650
But every time someone goes there now,

01:12:20.650 --> 01:12:21.782
they'll take a picture and then tag us-

01:12:21.782 --> 01:12:22.960
- They take a picture
and they tweet it at us,

01:12:22.960 --> 01:12:23.873
and we're like, please don't remind-

01:12:23.873 --> 01:12:25.204
- Just the shame just gets more

01:12:25.204 --> 01:12:26.037
every time.
- No, but I've always thought

01:12:26.037 --> 01:12:29.330
like Japanese artists have
such amazing signatures,

01:12:29.330 --> 01:12:32.200
and they're all good at drawing.

01:12:32.200 --> 01:12:36.330
And so I've always felt like
that's a huge complex for me.

01:12:36.330 --> 01:12:39.890
Like, why is everyone so
good at like autographs?

01:12:39.890 --> 01:12:41.992
- But a signature-
- Is there a class?

01:12:41.992 --> 01:12:44.530
- That's why I was genuinely curious.

01:12:44.530 --> 01:12:45.910
Do you guys practice this shit?

01:12:45.910 --> 01:12:47.013
'Cause I had to make mine up on the spot,

01:12:47.013 --> 01:12:49.410
and that's why mine looks complete arse.

01:12:49.410 --> 01:12:52.290
- I've never just practice or like-

01:12:52.290 --> 01:12:54.983
- Yeah, I'm still trying
to figure that out.

01:12:54.983 --> 01:12:56.910
- Because I feel like when we all

01:12:56.910 --> 01:12:59.110
like first had to do signatures, right,

01:12:59.110 --> 01:13:00.510
it kind of came out of the blue.

01:13:00.510 --> 01:13:01.343
Like you weren't expecting it.

01:13:01.343 --> 01:13:03.480
- I feel like a signature
shouldn't be a burden.

01:13:03.480 --> 01:13:05.790
And when I ask a Japanese
person to do a signature,

01:13:05.790 --> 01:13:07.260
it's like, give me 15 minutes

01:13:07.260 --> 01:13:09.710
and a Red Bull and I'll be
done. It's like, no, no, no, no,

01:13:09.710 --> 01:13:10.780
you can just do like some squiggles.

01:13:10.780 --> 01:13:12.910
I don't care, just slap
it, I don't know, what.

01:13:12.910 --> 01:13:15.110
I feel bad when they're drawings
something really delicate,

01:13:15.110 --> 01:13:18.740
and I'm like, this is just
gonna be in my wall somewhere.

01:13:18.740 --> 01:13:20.190
- I think at the highest pressure for me

01:13:20.190 --> 01:13:22.640
is signing a shikishi, 'cause a shikishi,

01:13:22.640 --> 01:13:24.810
there's a lot of white
space in those shikishi.

01:13:24.810 --> 01:13:27.480
And there's only so many
ways I can make it look good.

01:13:27.480 --> 01:13:30.280
So like, when I have to
throw my signature big,

01:13:30.280 --> 01:13:35.010
it's like enlarging a
100-by-100 pixel image.

01:13:35.010 --> 01:13:38.570
It's like Minecraft quality
that we're talking about.

01:13:38.570 --> 01:13:42.170
It's like 360 YouTube
and it just looks bad.

01:13:42.170 --> 01:13:43.290
- Because we're so used to doing

01:13:43.290 --> 01:13:45.260
in like the corner of an anime poster

01:13:45.260 --> 01:13:47.343
so that it doesn't go over it, right?

01:13:47.343 --> 01:13:51.530
- So I, ever since I
made a debut, in Japan,

01:13:51.530 --> 01:13:56.070
I've had to have shikishi
signatures often.

01:13:56.070 --> 01:13:59.620
And one advice from me
is how to fill it up

01:13:59.620 --> 01:14:01.083
is just draw a lot of stars.

01:14:02.355 --> 01:14:03.900
- Just a lot of stars?
- Yeah, that's why

01:14:03.900 --> 01:14:05.490
my shikishi's always filled with stars,

01:14:05.490 --> 01:14:08.200
because I don't know what
to do with the white space.

01:14:08.200 --> 01:14:09.170
- Yeah, but that's the problem, right?

01:14:09.170 --> 01:14:10.600
Is that we have three people

01:14:10.600 --> 01:14:12.800
who just cannot draw to save their life.

01:14:12.800 --> 01:14:14.080
So it's just like-
- Same here.

01:14:14.080 --> 01:14:16.144
- Do I like draw an anime character?

01:14:16.144 --> 01:14:18.370
But I don't wanna get
like DeviantArt-quality

01:14:18.370 --> 01:14:20.263
anime character next to my signature,

01:14:20.263 --> 01:14:21.290
so it's like, what do I,

01:14:21.290 --> 01:14:23.110
so that's why, at least with my signature,

01:14:23.110 --> 01:14:26.250
my one saving grace was
just like the cat face.

01:14:26.250 --> 01:14:28.400
I have to add something
to this to make it unique.

01:14:28.400 --> 01:14:31.440
And one thing I've always found
with like Japanese artists

01:14:31.440 --> 01:14:33.150
or like just voice actors or whoever

01:14:33.150 --> 01:14:37.170
is that they always have
like their mark of identity.

01:14:37.170 --> 01:14:38.230
I'm just like, what's it for me?

01:14:38.230 --> 01:14:39.450
I'll just put a fucking cat face on it.

01:14:39.450 --> 01:14:42.360
- I think the reason like
Japanese artists and entertainers

01:14:44.010 --> 01:14:46.050
have sort of artwork with their signatures

01:14:46.050 --> 01:14:48.016
is because they have to sign shikishi,

01:14:48.016 --> 01:14:49.616
and they have to fill up that white space.

01:14:49.616 --> 01:14:51.720
- Yeah, yeah.
- Exactly, yeah.

01:14:51.720 --> 01:14:53.220
- Basically, just put a cat face

01:14:53.220 --> 01:14:55.250
or make up an emoji apparently.

01:14:55.250 --> 01:14:57.790
- Or a star or something.
- Or just lots of stars.

01:14:57.790 --> 01:15:00.680
This is a problem that 99% of viewers

01:15:00.680 --> 01:15:02.573
will have zero relationship with.

01:15:04.520 --> 01:15:06.620
- Relatable topic.
- First World problem.

01:15:09.120 --> 01:15:11.070
- So you grew up in the US

01:15:11.070 --> 01:15:12.650
your whole life.
- Yes, exactly.

01:15:12.650 --> 01:15:15.418
- When did you come to
Japan for the first time?

01:15:15.418 --> 01:15:17.790
- I've been coming back to Japan,

01:15:17.790 --> 01:15:20.261
like pretty much every year
when I was little, just-

01:15:20.261 --> 01:15:22.630
- With your parents.
- Just to go to my

01:15:22.630 --> 01:15:24.480
grandparents' house and stuff.

01:15:24.480 --> 01:15:29.480
And then I went to, I came
to Japan in middle school,

01:15:29.550 --> 01:15:32.760
and I experienced
Japanese school education

01:15:32.760 --> 01:15:34.000
for the first time in my life.

01:15:34.000 --> 01:15:35.118
- How was that going for an American?

01:15:35.118 --> 01:15:36.577
- Hell.
- Hell?

01:15:36.577 --> 01:15:38.150
But why?

01:15:38.150 --> 01:15:39.450
- It was completely hell for me,

01:15:39.450 --> 01:15:41.530
because even though I can speak

01:15:41.530 --> 01:15:43.800
regular sort of everyday Japanese,

01:15:43.800 --> 01:15:46.773
I couldn't read or write up to par.

01:15:48.390 --> 01:15:49.223
- Am I allowed to ask this,

01:15:49.223 --> 01:15:51.220
but why were you going to school in Japan?

01:15:51.220 --> 01:15:52.330
Like, was there a reason why?

01:15:52.330 --> 01:15:54.419
- Well, that's the music thing.

01:15:54.419 --> 01:15:55.278
- Okay.
- Oh.

01:15:55.278 --> 01:15:56.570
- I wanted to become a musician in Japan,

01:15:56.570 --> 01:15:58.850
so I came to Japan to do music,

01:15:58.850 --> 01:16:01.520
and I still have to go to
school, so I went to school,

01:16:01.520 --> 01:16:04.080
but I went to regular school,
which was a huge mistake.

01:16:04.080 --> 01:16:05.489
And I didn't go to an
international school,

01:16:05.489 --> 01:16:06.930
you know, that kind of thing.

01:16:06.930 --> 01:16:07.763
- How was that?

01:16:07.763 --> 01:16:08.870
Why was it a mistake?

01:16:08.870 --> 01:16:09.710
I'm curious.

01:16:09.710 --> 01:16:10.900
- It's just that I couldn't keep up

01:16:10.900 --> 01:16:15.070
with any of the education
and I was a complete loner.

01:16:15.070 --> 01:16:16.410
So I didn't have any friends-

01:16:16.410 --> 01:16:17.310
- I was gonna ask.

01:16:17.310 --> 01:16:18.410
Is it hard to make friends

01:16:18.410 --> 01:16:19.998
when you are like a transfer student?

01:16:19.998 --> 01:16:21.718
- I think it's impossible to make friends.

01:16:21.718 --> 01:16:22.551
- This is such a lie.

01:16:22.551 --> 01:16:24.012
Anime would have to believe
that the transfer student-

01:16:24.012 --> 01:16:25.988
- Yeah, they're like,
everyone is all over-

01:16:25.988 --> 01:16:28.977
- Everyone wants to know
the transfer student.

01:16:28.977 --> 01:16:31.250
Why would you lie to me, anime?

01:16:31.250 --> 01:16:32.360
- It's just like, there's that one scene

01:16:32.360 --> 01:16:35.170
where it's like a transfer
student from overseas

01:16:35.170 --> 01:16:36.750
who's like, oh, they can speak English.

01:16:36.750 --> 01:16:38.500
And then during the break,

01:16:38.500 --> 01:16:41.020
they're fuckin' all over
that transfer student.

01:16:41.020 --> 01:16:42.580
Did that happen to you at all?

01:16:42.580 --> 01:16:43.810
- Big surprise here.

01:16:43.810 --> 01:16:48.177
And I'm gonna give you a
huge sort of reality check,

01:16:48.177 --> 01:16:52.440
but as anime singer,
anime is not exactly real.

01:16:52.440 --> 01:16:53.273
- No!

01:16:56.095 --> 01:16:57.645
- I respect your opinion, I do.

01:16:58.569 --> 01:17:02.030
- But I'm gonna live in my anime reality.

01:17:02.030 --> 01:17:02.930
- I will choose to-

01:17:02.930 --> 01:17:06.100
- No, I hate to break it to
you guys, but no, no, but yeah.

01:17:06.100 --> 01:17:08.220
- You mean you didn't sit
in like the far corner

01:17:08.220 --> 01:17:10.850
of the classroom next to the window?

01:17:10.850 --> 01:17:14.870
- I was actually, since I came to Japan,

01:17:14.870 --> 01:17:17.890
and then I started the school

01:17:17.890 --> 01:17:20.770
at a very weird time in the sort of year,

01:17:20.770 --> 01:17:22.630
so I was like in the corner.

01:17:22.630 --> 01:17:24.420
And so I couldn't make friends

01:17:24.420 --> 01:17:27.820
and I couldn't keep up with
the studies and everything,

01:17:27.820 --> 01:17:29.630
like the culture was completely-

01:17:29.630 --> 01:17:30.513
- Right, right.
- Yeah,

01:17:30.513 --> 01:17:31.480
it's quite different from America.

01:17:31.480 --> 01:17:32.420
- I guess, for you as well,

01:17:32.420 --> 01:17:33.580
it's like doubly a pressure, right?

01:17:33.580 --> 01:17:35.010
Because you're full Japanese.

01:17:35.010 --> 01:17:37.053
- Everyone expects me to be Japanese.

01:17:38.730 --> 01:17:40.300
If I looked sort of American,

01:17:40.300 --> 01:17:44.770
probably people would be like,
nihongo daijoubu desu ka?

01:17:44.770 --> 01:17:47.950
But no, people would be
like completely normal.

01:17:47.950 --> 01:17:50.780
They expect me to understand
completely everything.

01:17:50.780 --> 01:17:54.560
So that was a huge source
of stress for me mentally.

01:17:54.560 --> 01:17:57.210
- Did you, how good was your
Japanese when you moved?

01:17:58.170 --> 01:18:00.500
- I could speak it,
but reading and writing

01:18:00.500 --> 01:18:02.650
was completely-
- So Japanese

01:18:02.650 --> 01:18:04.280
is technically your second language.

01:18:04.280 --> 01:18:05.113
- Yes, it's technically my second language

01:18:05.113 --> 01:18:06.990
and I didn't like actually

01:18:06.990 --> 01:18:09.115
officially study Japanese in America.

01:18:09.115 --> 01:18:10.117
- Right.
- Okay.

01:18:10.117 --> 01:18:13.740
- And so you were in Japanese
school until high school?

01:18:13.740 --> 01:18:16.972
- No, just for less
than two years, I think.

01:18:16.972 --> 01:18:17.805
- 'Cause you were like, thank God-

01:18:17.805 --> 01:18:19.890
- No, and then I just gave up

01:18:19.890 --> 01:18:21.580
and then I went back to the States

01:18:21.580 --> 01:18:23.150
and then I finished school there.

01:18:23.150 --> 01:18:25.060
And then after I finished school,

01:18:25.060 --> 01:18:28.940
I came to Japan and started my career.

01:18:28.940 --> 01:18:30.450
- Okay, what is the Japanese

01:18:30.450 --> 01:18:32.950
education system like compared to the US?

01:18:32.950 --> 01:18:36.810
Because I've thought about like, if,

01:18:36.810 --> 01:18:39.810
because I was also, I
was raised in the UK,

01:18:39.810 --> 01:18:41.830
that was where my education system is.

01:18:41.830 --> 01:18:44.140
I can't imagine having
an education in Asia,

01:18:44.140 --> 01:18:47.020
'cause the culture of the
Asian education system

01:18:47.020 --> 01:18:50.020
just seems like a lot of pressure.

01:18:50.020 --> 01:18:52.700
And that's something that
I'm not a fan of at all.

01:18:52.700 --> 01:18:57.700
- I think in Japan, I've only been

01:18:58.340 --> 01:18:59.890
as a student for less than two years,

01:18:59.890 --> 01:19:02.560
so I can't say I know
everything, but at the same time,

01:19:02.560 --> 01:19:05.270
I think they're very, like studying base.

01:19:05.270 --> 01:19:07.890
Everything is about
studying, studying, studying.

01:19:07.890 --> 01:19:12.890
And it's very difficult to be
a loner in school in Japan.

01:19:13.488 --> 01:19:17.730
You have to have your sort of niche,

01:19:17.730 --> 01:19:20.110
and you have to have your
place and you have to friends

01:19:20.110 --> 01:19:24.370
in order to really feel like-

01:19:24.370 --> 01:19:27.550
- So who are like the cool
kids in Japanese schools?

01:19:27.550 --> 01:19:28.760
Who are like the popular kids?

01:19:28.760 --> 01:19:30.284
'Cause in, like, when I was growing up,

01:19:30.284 --> 01:19:32.080
it would be like the people
who are good at sports

01:19:32.080 --> 01:19:34.332
like the jocks and stuff like that.

01:19:34.332 --> 01:19:36.000
Who is like, who are like,

01:19:36.000 --> 01:19:37.940
what makes you popular
in Japanese schools?

01:19:37.940 --> 01:19:39.780
I've always wondered about-

01:19:39.780 --> 01:19:41.520
- I think it is different in Japan.

01:19:41.520 --> 01:19:43.424
Like, it doesn't necessarily mean

01:19:43.424 --> 01:19:47.080
like you have to be the most
fashionable or anything,

01:19:47.080 --> 01:19:50.550
but in Japan it's more if you're outgoing

01:19:50.550 --> 01:19:53.763
and you're also smart educationally.

01:19:54.633 --> 01:19:56.503
- Well, that's one thing anime got right.

01:19:56.503 --> 01:19:57.480
- I noticed there's a big difference,

01:19:57.480 --> 01:19:59.470
because when I was growing up in the UK,

01:19:59.470 --> 01:20:00.410
if you did well on tests,

01:20:00.410 --> 01:20:02.820
that's like a black market.
- That's like you're bullied.

01:20:02.820 --> 01:20:05.060
- Like, whoa, you studied for an exam?

01:20:05.060 --> 01:20:07.130
Look at this fuckin' nerd.

01:20:07.130 --> 01:20:08.840
- Whereas in Japan, it's
like, whoa, you study?

01:20:08.840 --> 01:20:10.140
Oh my God, you're awesome.

01:20:11.738 --> 01:20:14.670
- So I think that kind
of thing is different.

01:20:14.670 --> 01:20:15.870
Like, if you're an all-rounder,

01:20:15.870 --> 01:20:17.500
if you're good at a
lot of different things

01:20:17.500 --> 01:20:21.020
and you're pretty much-
- The image of perfection.

01:20:21.020 --> 01:20:22.538
You're just good

01:20:22.538 --> 01:20:23.540
at everything.
- Like I said,

01:20:23.540 --> 01:20:24.580
Japan loves perfection.

01:20:24.580 --> 01:20:27.720
So I think they sort of exert perfection

01:20:27.720 --> 01:20:28.880
in the anime as well.

01:20:28.880 --> 01:20:33.880
Like the anime, they sort of
depict perfection in animation.

01:20:35.641 --> 01:20:36.474
- Yeah, I don't know if,

01:20:36.474 --> 01:20:38.610
you don't have to answer this
question if you don't want to,

01:20:38.610 --> 01:20:40.850
but did you ever have like
any negative experiences

01:20:40.850 --> 01:20:44.580
like bullying because
you are like foreign or-

01:20:44.580 --> 01:20:46.940
- There wasn't exactly
like direct bullying,

01:20:46.940 --> 01:20:50.520
but people didn't know how to
interact with me because they,

01:20:50.520 --> 01:20:52.010
because it wasn't an international school

01:20:52.010 --> 01:20:54.993
and they weren't exposed
to foreign people.

01:20:54.993 --> 01:20:57.560
