01:41:25.640 --> 01:41:29.980
And it depends if you are
the one that sort of offers,

01:41:29.980 --> 01:41:33.460
or they offer for you, it
depends on the situation.

01:41:33.460 --> 01:41:38.460
But once you sort of get an
offer or you go grab an offer,

01:41:41.390 --> 01:41:46.020
then that sort of starts into
the songwriting creation,

01:41:46.020 --> 01:41:47.740
and then-
- So you write all of it?

01:41:47.740 --> 01:41:50.250
- Yeah, you have to make
it from zero usually.

01:41:50.250 --> 01:41:52.010
So that begins there.

01:41:52.010 --> 01:41:54.490
And I wrote all the lyrics for my songs.

01:41:54.490 --> 01:41:57.425
Not all the melodies, but all the lyrics.

01:41:57.425 --> 01:41:59.265
- Do they give you any
input on any of that?

01:41:59.265 --> 01:42:00.098
Like the anime-

01:42:00.098 --> 01:42:02.210
- Do you have like any source material?

01:42:02.210 --> 01:42:03.630
Do you write around that, or was it just-

01:42:03.630 --> 01:42:05.180
- Usually, we start writing

01:42:05.180 --> 01:42:08.470
when the series isn't complete yet.

01:42:08.470 --> 01:42:13.030
So we only get like
really brief description.

01:42:13.030 --> 01:42:14.820
- So what was it like for
something like "BTOOOM!"?

01:42:14.820 --> 01:42:15.970
What do they say?

01:42:15.970 --> 01:42:18.620
- Oh, "BTOOOM!" was actually
a manga before the anime.

01:42:18.620 --> 01:42:20.477
So that really helps.
- You just read all the manga?

01:42:20.477 --> 01:42:24.930
- You read the manga and you
sort of, they also have hints,

01:42:24.930 --> 01:42:27.370
like this kind of song
or that kind of song,

01:42:27.370 --> 01:42:32.370
and then you try to fulfill
their expectations there.

01:42:32.650 --> 01:42:35.000
But "BTOOOM!", for example,
"No Pain, No Game,"

01:42:35.000 --> 01:42:37.000
we had a lot of freedom with that song.

01:42:37.000 --> 01:42:41.263
So they really probably didn't
expect that kind of sort of-

01:42:42.236 --> 01:42:44.823
- Upbeat-
- Kind of song.

01:42:46.240 --> 01:42:48.370
But everyone really like, so it stood out,

01:42:48.370 --> 01:42:50.350
in a good way I think, it stood out,

01:42:50.350 --> 01:42:52.100
and they were like, wow,

01:42:52.100 --> 01:42:53.740
we weren't expecting this in a good sense.

01:42:53.740 --> 01:42:56.010
- I think I can speak on
behalf of the anime community

01:42:56.010 --> 01:42:57.667
being like, most people-
- It's bangin'.

01:42:57.667 --> 01:43:01.400
- If not all people only remember
the openings of "BTOOOM!".

01:43:01.400 --> 01:43:04.690
- So is that like a one-take,
here's a song, I'm done,

01:43:04.690 --> 01:43:06.680
or is it like, they constantly are always,

01:43:06.680 --> 01:43:08.550
can you change this, can you
change this, can we try this?

01:43:08.550 --> 01:43:11.980
- Sometimes they have very like detailed

01:43:13.820 --> 01:43:15.670
sort of descriptions for what they want,

01:43:15.670 --> 01:43:17.480
but sometimes, it's just completely free.

01:43:17.480 --> 01:43:21.210
So with "BTOOOM!" though,
we had a lot of freedom,

01:43:21.210 --> 01:43:24.890
so we didn't have to adjust
or redo a lot of things.

01:43:24.890 --> 01:43:26.620
But for other songs, for example,

01:43:26.620 --> 01:43:31.620
there are a couple of
retakes or recreations,

01:43:32.560 --> 01:43:36.940
or there are some songs that
I've done, I've written,

01:43:36.940 --> 01:43:40.780
that have completely
disappeared after it's cleared.

01:43:40.780 --> 01:43:42.800
- So when you do an anime opening,

01:43:42.800 --> 01:43:45.080
who owns the rights to that song?

01:43:45.080 --> 01:43:46.500
Is it the, did the anime people

01:43:46.500 --> 01:43:47.333
just get like a license to use it

01:43:47.333 --> 01:43:49.770
in the anime and you retain everything?

01:43:49.770 --> 01:43:51.130
Or like, how does that work, if you know?

01:43:51.130 --> 01:43:52.540
- It might be the label, right?

01:43:52.540 --> 01:43:53.540
- It's probably the label.
- I think the label

01:43:53.540 --> 01:43:54.373
has the song.
- Yeah, you're just like,

01:43:54.373 --> 01:43:56.147
I don't know, I make music.

01:43:56.147 --> 01:43:58.320
- The label has the song rights.

01:43:58.320 --> 01:44:00.592
And so when the song is used,

01:44:00.592 --> 01:44:02.300
the rights belong to the label.

01:44:02.300 --> 01:44:03.670
- Because I think flying DOG was like,

01:44:03.670 --> 01:44:04.730
you can correct me if I'm wrong,

01:44:04.730 --> 01:44:07.130
it's like a major label that was primarily

01:44:07.130 --> 01:44:08.840
focused on like more anime music.

01:44:08.840 --> 01:44:12.260
So a lot of anime OSTs and openings

01:44:12.260 --> 01:44:16.890
were usually started and
owned by that record label.

01:44:16.890 --> 01:44:17.723
So like-

01:44:17.723 --> 01:44:19.370
- I like how you're looking at Connor

01:44:19.370 --> 01:44:23.081
like he's gonna know what
you're talking about. (laughs)

01:44:23.081 --> 01:44:25.697
I'm telling you because
you probably don't know.

01:44:25.697 --> 01:44:27.474
- Fuckin' hurt.
- I'm just telling,

01:44:27.474 --> 01:44:29.957
because I was, again, like I
was reading your Wikipedia,

01:44:29.957 --> 01:44:31.360
and you know, flying
DOG and stuff like that.

01:44:31.360 --> 01:44:33.119
- I did a bit of research.
- Yeah, I did,

01:44:33.119 --> 01:44:34.911
I did a bit of research.

01:44:34.911 --> 01:44:37.050
'Cause I was always interested
as well of like how,

01:44:37.050 --> 01:44:41.130
I guess, like rights and
distribution works for anime songs,

01:44:41.130 --> 01:44:42.930
because I feel it's completely different

01:44:42.930 --> 01:44:44.976
to like an artist just
releasing their own album.

01:44:44.976 --> 01:44:45.960
- Yeah, I always
wondered, 'cause you know,

01:44:45.960 --> 01:44:50.540
a lot of the songs wouldn't blow up

01:44:50.540 --> 01:44:51.840
without the anime to back of it.

01:44:51.840 --> 01:44:53.630
So I wondered if there
was a system that like,

01:44:53.630 --> 01:44:54.710
there's a co-ownership, or like,

01:44:54.710 --> 01:44:56.000
I'm just pretty intrigued.

01:44:56.000 --> 01:44:57.050
I didn't know if you knew.

01:44:57.050 --> 01:44:58.920
- Yeah, it's very complicated.

01:44:58.920 --> 01:45:00.630
Like the rights thing is just-

01:45:00.630 --> 01:45:03.010
- It sounds like nightmare.
- It is a nightmare.

01:45:03.010 --> 01:45:04.340
- I've always had issues,

01:45:04.340 --> 01:45:06.690
like YouTube issues with like
rights and it's always a mess.

01:45:06.690 --> 01:45:10.380
- You know in Japan, everything
about rights is huge.

01:45:10.380 --> 01:45:14.056
You can't say certain stuff on TV.

01:45:14.056 --> 01:45:16.570
You need permission for a lot of things.

01:45:16.570 --> 01:45:18.790
- Yeah, we've experienced it.
- Yeah, you can imagine.

01:45:18.790 --> 01:45:21.497
- The Japan fucking do
you have permission hell.

01:45:21.497 --> 01:45:23.530
It's just like never ending.

01:45:23.530 --> 01:45:26.850
- The approval chain is
just fuckin' a mile along.

01:45:26.850 --> 01:45:28.693
- I never, like, there
were so many things,

01:45:28.693 --> 01:45:32.460
since working with Japanese
companies that I notice.

01:45:32.460 --> 01:45:35.415
I was like, oh, you
need approval for that?

01:45:35.415 --> 01:45:37.610
- 'Cause it was the first time that I had,

01:45:37.610 --> 01:45:42.173
that I experienced taking off
a label of a water bottle,

01:45:43.330 --> 01:45:45.680
to drink it in front of media.

01:45:45.680 --> 01:45:47.970
In America, I never
even thought about that.

01:45:47.970 --> 01:45:50.063
- So yes, I openly drink Evian water.

01:45:51.020 --> 01:45:55.430
- So taking the labels
off at events or like,

01:45:55.430 --> 01:45:58.410
that is completely Japanese culture.

01:45:58.410 --> 01:45:59.800
- I notice that the first time actually,

01:45:59.800 --> 01:46:01.690
when I was watching
like a Japanese TV show,

01:46:01.690 --> 01:46:04.140
and I noticed that the water bottle

01:46:04.140 --> 01:46:07.700
on the desk or whatever
was like mosaicked out.

01:46:07.700 --> 01:46:10.098
And I'm like, what the
fuck are they drinking?

01:46:10.098 --> 01:46:13.010
How bad is it-
- Is this hentai water

01:46:13.010 --> 01:46:14.596
I'm drinking, like loli water?

01:46:14.596 --> 01:46:17.340
- What is in this water
that they have to sensor it?

01:46:17.340 --> 01:46:20.500
- They'll show you shots on
TV, and it'd be like Shibuya,

01:46:20.500 --> 01:46:24.820
and everything is blurred
except like two people walking.

01:46:24.820 --> 01:46:26.379
Why are you even showing this?

01:46:26.379 --> 01:46:28.627
They're not showing anything.

01:46:28.627 --> 01:46:30.480
All the brands in Shibuya
and all the billboards

01:46:30.480 --> 01:46:31.827
have to be like blurred out.

01:46:31.827 --> 01:46:33.743
- Looks like a JAV shoot in Shibuya.

01:46:35.310 --> 01:46:36.620
- It's odd, 'cause then two seconds later,

01:46:36.620 --> 01:46:38.110
it'll cut to a shot
where everything's shown.

01:46:38.110 --> 01:46:40.830
And I'm like, there's
no consistency on this.

01:46:40.830 --> 01:46:41.663
I'm so confused.

01:46:41.663 --> 01:46:43.110
Now there must be some rights going on

01:46:43.110 --> 01:46:44.890
where it's completely
flip-flopping in that.

01:46:44.890 --> 01:46:46.030
Yeah, I don't know, it's bizarre.

01:46:46.030 --> 01:46:49.030
- How did it feel, like the
first time you watched an anime

01:46:49.030 --> 01:46:51.910
and just heard yourself singing
before the anime started?

01:46:51.910 --> 01:46:55.198
- Oh yeah, it was really nerve-wracking.

01:46:55.198 --> 01:46:58.393
I was probably peeing
my pants waiting for it.

01:46:58.393 --> 01:47:00.550
- 'Cause you're pretty much living

01:47:00.550 --> 01:47:01.950
the dream that I think a lot of like,

01:47:01.950 --> 01:47:03.410
especially Western weebs one,

01:47:03.410 --> 01:47:05.320
where they're like, yeah, I can sing.

01:47:05.320 --> 01:47:08.450
One day, I'm gonna sing
in an anime opening.

01:47:08.450 --> 01:47:11.070
- It's very surreal, it's very surreal.

01:47:11.070 --> 01:47:15.020
It didn't really like hit
home until a lot later.

01:47:15.020 --> 01:47:17.730
- 'Cause do you, I assume when
you are producing the song,

01:47:17.730 --> 01:47:21.013
you don't actually get to
see the animation opening

01:47:21.013 --> 01:47:22.629
of like what they put to your song.

01:47:22.629 --> 01:47:23.950
- So exactly the first time that,

01:47:23.950 --> 01:47:27.810
well, actually, I did see
like a sample of the opening,

01:47:27.810 --> 01:47:29.140
but the first time I actually saw

01:47:29.140 --> 01:47:32.850
the official finalized version was on TV.

01:47:32.850 --> 01:47:35.370
So it was probably like
the same as you guys.

01:47:35.370 --> 01:47:36.680
I was like in front of the screen,

01:47:36.680 --> 01:47:38.553
I was like, what the hell?

01:47:39.811 --> 01:47:41.980
- What the hell is happening?

01:47:41.980 --> 01:47:43.653
- I hear my voice from the TV.

01:47:44.568 --> 01:47:46.210
- Do you normally skip anime openings?

01:47:46.210 --> 01:47:47.360
Am I allowed-

01:47:47.360 --> 01:47:49.190
- Um, I usually, sometimes.

01:47:51.170 --> 01:47:53.454
But most of the time-
- Industry secret.

01:47:53.454 --> 01:47:57.253
- Sometimes, yeah, I try to watch it.

01:47:58.423 --> 01:48:01.020
If I like it, though,
I'll watch it definitely.

01:48:01.020 --> 01:48:02.010
- Yeah, I mean, I don't think

01:48:02.010 --> 01:48:03.570
there's anything wrong with
skipping anime openings.

01:48:03.570 --> 01:48:04.920
Yeah, I said it, I fuckin' said it.

01:48:04.920 --> 01:48:07.090
- Yeah, sometimes they're kind of mid.

01:48:07.090 --> 01:48:08.800
- Yeah, let's be honest.

01:48:08.800 --> 01:48:10.220
- What can you say?
- As an artist, right,

01:48:10.220 --> 01:48:12.660
when Netflix gives you
that skip intro button,

01:48:12.660 --> 01:48:13.897
does your heart like
die inside a little bit?

01:48:13.897 --> 01:48:15.690
You're like, oh, not my hard work.

01:48:15.690 --> 01:48:18.440
- I try to not imagine how
many people are skipping my-

01:48:20.190 --> 01:48:22.203
- How dare you skip my banger song?

01:48:23.410 --> 01:48:24.990
- Because now that you
work in the industry,

01:48:24.990 --> 01:48:27.400
has that changed the way you kind of like

01:48:27.400 --> 01:48:29.950
not only view anime music,
but just music in general?

01:48:29.950 --> 01:48:32.530
'Cause like, as someone
who works in anime YouTube,

01:48:32.530 --> 01:48:34.580
I can't look at anime YouTube as the same.

01:48:34.580 --> 01:48:37.643
Or like I can't view it as just,

01:48:37.643 --> 01:48:39.260
to be entertained anymore.

01:48:39.260 --> 01:48:42.450
I can't shut off that part of my brain.

01:48:42.450 --> 01:48:44.690
- I think it has sort of destroyed a bit

01:48:44.690 --> 01:48:47.480
of like the enjoyment part of it.

01:48:47.480 --> 01:48:50.790
Because everything that concerns music

01:48:50.790 --> 01:48:52.790
right now becomes a job for me.

01:48:52.790 --> 01:48:55.653
So I start listening to like,

01:48:55.653 --> 01:48:58.987
it's hard to just listen to it
for my enjoyment, I do find.

01:48:58.987 --> 01:49:01.030
- 'Cause sometimes you see someone

01:49:01.030 --> 01:49:03.200
who does something fuckin'
great and you're just like,

01:49:03.200 --> 01:49:05.120
damn it, I wish I did that,

01:49:05.120 --> 01:49:08.520
I wish I could be that.
- God, I wish that was me.

01:49:08.520 --> 01:49:09.760
Yeah, I get that every time.

01:49:09.760 --> 01:49:11.210
I'm just like-
- Why didn't I

01:49:11.210 --> 01:49:13.330
come up with that?
- Yeah, exactly, right?

01:49:13.330 --> 01:49:14.163
Exactly.
- It's like,

01:49:14.163 --> 01:49:15.170
I love this video,

01:49:15.170 --> 01:49:17.640
except for the fact that I didn't make it.

01:49:17.640 --> 01:49:18.990
Like, I wish I'd had made that.

01:49:18.990 --> 01:49:21.240
- Yeah, I mean, I love you-
- I was going to do it.

01:49:21.240 --> 01:49:22.430
But they got to it before me.

01:49:22.430 --> 01:49:24.000
- But this person did it before me.

01:49:24.000 --> 01:49:25.190
God damn, I hate this person,

01:49:25.190 --> 01:49:26.801
but I fuckin' respect this person.

01:49:26.801 --> 01:49:29.677
- They fuckin' stole the idea.
That was just in my head.

01:49:29.677 --> 01:49:32.780
Is there like, I guess,
like very general question,

01:49:32.780 --> 01:49:35.100
is there like a Japanese
artist that you would ever

01:49:35.100 --> 01:49:36.980
wanna like collaborate with in the future?

01:49:36.980 --> 01:49:40.380
- Oh, there are so many,
but especially recently,

01:49:40.380 --> 01:49:43.190
I feel that I want to
do more collaborations.

01:49:43.190 --> 01:49:45.883
And so you know,

01:49:48.240 --> 01:49:50.808
like there are a lot of artists.

01:49:50.808 --> 01:49:52.383
- I don't think we asked,

01:49:52.383 --> 01:49:56.339
like who are some artists
that you like or respect?

01:49:56.339 --> 01:49:57.970
- Japanese or Western.

01:49:57.970 --> 01:49:59.738
- Japanese or Western, well, you know, I-

01:49:59.738 --> 01:50:01.680
- Avril Lavigne, of course.
- Avril Lavigne.

01:50:01.680 --> 01:50:02.669
Right up there at the top.
- Avril Lavigne.

01:50:02.669 --> 01:50:03.502
You have to live up to that.

01:50:03.502 --> 01:50:06.260
No, but I do really respect her music,

01:50:06.260 --> 01:50:09.003
but also like artists like Miyavi.

01:50:10.700 --> 01:50:15.040
Oh, but one amazing thing
that happened recently,

01:50:15.040 --> 01:50:18.850
is I collaborated on stage with FLOW.

01:50:18.850 --> 01:50:19.980
- Oh, wow.

01:50:19.980 --> 01:50:22.540
- So that was a real
dream come true for me.

01:50:22.540 --> 01:50:27.540
So that was amazing because
I was a listener of theirs.

01:50:27.697 --> 01:50:29.046
- How did that happen?

01:50:29.046 --> 01:50:30.875
- I have no idea.

01:50:30.875 --> 01:50:33.214
- You just turned up to
perform and Flo is right there?

01:50:33.214 --> 01:50:35.470
- What was like, let
us introduce ourselves.

01:50:35.470 --> 01:50:38.550
- I woke up and I was collaborating
on stage with Flo, no.

01:50:38.550 --> 01:50:42.700
No, but it was an event,
and it was an event,

01:50:42.700 --> 01:50:46.210
and the event side said that, hey,

01:50:46.210 --> 01:50:47.820
it would be great if you collaborated

01:50:47.820 --> 01:50:49.920
on a cover song with FLOW,

01:50:49.920 --> 01:50:52.970
which was "Sanbun no
Ichi Junjou na Kanjou,"

01:50:52.970 --> 01:50:56.390
which was a "Rurouni
Kenshin" anime opening.

01:50:56.390 --> 01:50:58.550
So that was amazing.

01:50:58.550 --> 01:51:01.600
But the thing is, we
met for the first time

01:51:01.600 --> 01:51:04.680
during the only rehearsal that happened

01:51:04.680 --> 01:51:07.063
right before the actual stage.

01:51:08.150 --> 01:51:10.410
So that, we didn't have a lot of time

01:51:10.410 --> 01:51:14.830
to get to know each other
more, but it was amazing.

01:51:14.830 --> 01:51:17.050
And these kind of miracles do happen

01:51:17.050 --> 01:51:18.670
when you're working like this.

01:51:18.670 --> 01:51:21.540
So that's always exciting.

01:51:21.540 --> 01:51:23.637
- And it seems like you've just,

01:51:23.637 --> 01:51:25.570
had a lot of great opportunities

01:51:25.570 --> 01:51:27.042
that you never kind of like aim for,

01:51:27.042 --> 01:51:28.290
It just kind of happens.

01:51:28.290 --> 01:51:30.530
- That definitely, I'd have to say

01:51:30.530 --> 01:51:33.030
that a lot of the miracles that happened

01:51:33.030 --> 01:51:34.567
were unexpected in my career.

01:51:34.567 --> 01:51:35.620
- The next step for you though

01:51:35.620 --> 01:51:38.134
is collaborating with Avril Lavigne.

01:51:38.134 --> 01:51:42.287
- Ah, let's see if we can make it happen.

01:51:44.070 --> 01:51:47.500
- So I have to ask, do
you watch any YouTubers?

01:51:47.500 --> 01:51:50.280
- I have made a YouTube watching debut.

01:51:50.280 --> 01:51:53.000
So I'm just a newbie right now.

01:51:53.000 --> 01:51:55.810
So I'm starting to
search for good channels.

01:51:55.810 --> 01:51:58.720
And I actually, I'm planning

01:51:58.720 --> 01:52:01.210
to start my own channel as well.

01:52:01.210 --> 01:52:02.460
I'm still studying right now.

01:52:02.460 --> 01:52:04.070
I'm watching you guys and I'm-

01:52:04.070 --> 01:52:05.720
- Well, I can't sing.

01:52:06.853 --> 01:52:08.556
I do cosplay badly.

01:52:08.556 --> 01:52:10.460
What are you gonna do
in your YouTube channel?

01:52:10.460 --> 01:52:12.850
- Just, mostly like half of the things

01:52:12.850 --> 01:52:14.670
I plan to do are gonna be music-based,

01:52:14.670 --> 01:52:17.630
but half of the things are
going to be like just for fun,

01:52:17.630 --> 01:52:22.610
just for having fun with my
watchers and me being me.

01:52:22.610 --> 01:52:25.465
So yeah, any advice?

01:52:25.465 --> 01:52:28.290
- Oh, that's a loaded
question right there.

01:52:28.290 --> 01:52:29.690
- You gotta get a clickbait.

01:52:31.660 --> 01:52:34.030
You singing, just make it sound crazy.

01:52:34.030 --> 01:52:36.223
- Yeah.
- I sang every song ever.

01:52:37.240 --> 01:52:40.843
- Titles and thumbnails are
like your bread and butter.

01:52:40.843 --> 01:52:42.923
- If you don't have a catchy-
- What do you recommend then?

